{"id":"e05t4","name":"Card Velocity Alerts","lang":"python","entry":"solution","params":["transactions","max_count","window"],"limit_s":4,"ordered":true,"desc":"<p>The fraud team blocks cards that are used too often in a short time. You are given <code>transactions</code>, a list of <code>[card_id, timestamp, status]</code> where <code>timestamp</code> is a number of seconds written as a string and <code>status</code> is <code>\"approved\"</code> or <code>\"declined\"</code>. Transactions are <b>not sorted</b>.</p>\n<p>Both approved and declined transactions count. A card triggers an alert as soon as it has <b>more than</b> <code>max_count</code> transactions inside a time window of <code>window</code> seconds, which means: there are <code>max_count + 1</code> transactions of the card whose timestamps <code>t1 &lt;= ... &lt;= tk</code> satisfy <code>tk - t1 &lt; window</code>.</p>\n<p>Your task is to return, for every card that triggers an alert, a pair <code>[card_id, alert_at]</code>, where <code>alert_at</code> is the timestamp (as a string) of the transaction that triggers the <b>first</b> alert of the card. Sort by <code>alert_at</code> as a number, then by <code>card_id</code>.</p>\n<h4>Example</h4><p>For <code>transactions = [[\"c1\", \"130\", \"approved\"], [\"c2\", \"100\", \"approved\"], [\"c1\", \"100\", \"declined\"], [\"c2\", \"160\", \"approved\"], [\"c1\", \"159\", \"approved\"], [\"c2\", \"130\", \"declined\"]], max_count = 2, window = 60</code>, the output should be</p><pre class=\"exv\">[[\"c1\", \"159\"]]</pre>\n<p>With <code>max_count = 2</code> and <code>window = 60</code>, card <code>c1</code> has 3 transactions at <code>100</code>, <code>130</code> and <code>159</code>: <code>159 - 100 &lt; 60</code>, so the alert is at <code>159</code>. Card <code>c2</code> has 3 transactions but <code>160 - 100</code> is not less than <code>60</code>.</p><div class=\"lim\"><b>[execution time limit]</b> 4 seconds (py3)<br><b>[memory limit]</b> 1 GB<br><b>[input]</b> array.array.string transactions<br><b>[input]</b> integer max_count<br><b>[input]</b> integer window<br><b>[output]</b> array.array.string</div>","starter":"def solution(transactions, max_count, window):\n    # write your code here\n    return []\n","hints":[],"summary_fr":"","tags":["fenêtre glissante","deux pointeurs","tri par carte","bornes incluses"],"minutes":22,"source":"Kata Lab","files":null,"visible":[{"input":{"transactions":[["c1","130","approved"],["c2","100","approved"],["c1","100","declined"],["c2","160","approved"],["c1","159","approved"],["c2","130","declined"]],"max_count":2,"window":60},"expected":{"value":[["c1","159"]]}},{"input":{"transactions":[["b","5","approved"],["a","9","approved"],["a","10","approved"],["b","5","approved"],["z","1000","approved"]],"max_count":1,"window":1},"expected":{"value":[["b","5"]]}}],"hidden_n":9,"hidden":"","solution":""}